# r3e final verification
# 2026-10-16T05:42:17Z

DEFECT FIXED
  search/verify_outputs.py rule 2 required every file in the R1 output
  directory to be named in MANIFEST.json. A .DS_Store created by Finder
  was therefore counted as an unmanifested file; the bundle failed
  validation; validate_r1 correctly refused to read a scientific result
  from a bundle that failed validation; and II1-SEARCH-R1 reported

      FAILED - "R1 evidence failed validation, so no scientific result
      was read from it: .DS_Store is present but not named in the
      manifest."

  which made II-1_BASELINE_RECONSTRUCTION FAILED instead of PARTIAL and
  suppressed a real finding (the released search returning 2
  epsilon-close differences where the README documents one).

  The operator's evidence was intact throughout. Every digest named in
  MANIFEST.json matched before and after.

  This was an inconsistency in this adapter: evaluation_gate already had
  the correct policy in BENIGN_UNTRACKED - OS/interpreter files are
  recorded, do not block, and are never deleted - and the operator had
  just seen it work ("untracked-benign=2:.DS_Store,__pycache__/",
  "LEFT IN PLACE"). The R1 validator never received the same policy, so
  two validators in one adapter disagreed about what counts as evidence.

FIX
  verify_outputs.py: BENIGN_NAMES / BENIGN_DIRS / BENIGN_SUFFIXES and
  _is_benign(), mirroring evaluation_gate. Debris is excused, RECORDED in
  summary["unmanifested_benign"] with a note, and left on disk. Matching
  is on path PARTS, not substrings. Manifested files are hash-checked as
  before, whatever they are named.

  implementation_stages.py: validate_r1() carries the benign list up, and
  the II1-SEARCH-R1 component adds the note to its own limitations so the
  record DISCLOSES the debris rather than passing silently.

